# Testing Rules

- Test observable behavior, not implementation details alone.
- Cover successful behavior, invalid input, authorization failures, and relevant edge cases.
- Prefer deterministic tests that do not require AWS.
- Run the smallest relevant test first, then broader checks appropriate to the change.
- If a check is unavailable or not run, say so clearly. Never weaken assertions just to make a test pass.
